      "writtenOn": "2020-03-20T15:57:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I *think* I understand what this means (XORKeyStream crypts fewer blocks when it would otherwise overflow), but it\u0027s a bit vague. And doesn\u0027t s.buf also cause XORKeyStream to be non-constant-time, irrespective of the counter value?",
      "revId": "c37b6fcac938baaee70c4440431444de39aeb17c",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "873372dd_09bbe2fc",
        "filename": "chacha20/chacha_generic.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 11715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-20T18:22:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, no XORKeyStream implementation can be constant-time relative to the order of calls, but what this is saying is that if you set the counter to 0xffffffff the next XORKeyStream call will take a different time than if you set it to a lower value, because we use a different implementation.\n\nI agree it\u0027s not super clear but I don\u0027t know how else to word it, and accept suggestions.",
      "parentUuid": "75aa0e86_2b022228",
      "revId": "c37b6fcac938baaee70c4440431444de39aeb17c",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c6dc65f_370980cc",
        "filename": "chacha20/chacha_generic.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 24748
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-20T23:25:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it necessary to document this at all? XORKeyStream isn\u0027t claimed to be constant time anyway, so this warning feels redundant. If anything, maybe put a warning on XORKeyStream.",
      "parentUuid": "873372dd_09bbe2fc",
      "revId": "c37b6fcac938baaee70c4440431444de39aeb17c",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9eb3190e_26f59bfe",
        "filename": "chacha20/chacha_generic.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 11715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-21T01:40:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A caller that makes differently-sized calls to XORKeyStream is responsible for the variance so is definitely aware of it, but it would be reasonable to expect that the value passed to SetCounter doesn\u0027t leak through side channels, which instead it does.\n\nFor example, if the QUIC counter value were secret we\u0027d have a problem here.",
      "parentUuid": "6c6dc65f_370980cc",
      "revId": "c37b6fcac938baaee70c4440431444de39aeb17c",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": true
    },
